fferential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-4)y(-4)+x(2)y(2)+x(4)y(4).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=k-2t$ and $q(t)=5-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-4)q(-4)+p(2)q(2)+p(4)q(4) \\\\  & =(k+8)(5-8)+(k-4)(5-2)+(k-8)(5-8) \\\\  & =(-3k-24)+(3k-12)+(-3k+24) \\\\  & =-3k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3k-12 & =0 \\\\ 3k & =-12 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7396538f8f1f0b2bdd74e07b30da8954a002935ee83ef407b4fd5e2a25132f1" "basis" 1456 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/edb-import/verification.json"}