ion" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-12"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "15"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-4)y(-4)+x(2)y(2)+x(4)y(4).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=k-2t$ and $q(t)=5-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-4)q(-4)+p(2)q(2)+p(4)q(4) \\\\  & =(k+8)(5-8)+(k-4)(5-2)+(k-8)(5-8) \\\\  & =(-3k-24)+(3k-12)+(-3k+24) \\\\  & =-3k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3k-12 & =0 \\\\ 3k & =-12 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93f46b449376cefaf77dd465a16c29685f2f7472b888ef2bccc4151a27c1076d"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1)+\\frac{1}{10}x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=3+t$ and $q(t)=3t-k{t}^{2}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(0)q(0)+2p(1)q(1)+\\frac{1}{10}p(2)q(2) \\\\  & =(3+0)(0)+(3+1)(3-k)+\\frac{1}{10}(3+2)(6-4k) \\\\  & =0+(12-4k)+(3-2k) \\\\  & =15-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 15-6k & =0 \\\\ 6k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93f46b449376cefaf77dd465a16c29685f2f7472b888ef2bccc4151a27c1076d"} {"question" "q-97360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057597/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a16d55411c15b12569d8cfef2cc3d047c6c28c7398419f768ec62abfa94729e"} {"question" "q-97360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\fr